# ironworks — public repo of the platform, not our live deployment.
# Credentials, infra addresses, private chat ids, and internal records must never be
# committed. .gitignore only stops new commits — it can't scrub history or a secret
# embedded in a tracked file (parameterize those).
#
# Comments here state the CLASS withheld, never the instance: a rule that explains
# itself by describing what it hides hands the reader the thing it is hiding.
# Delete a rule and its file together — an entry that outlives its reason stops gating.

# Credentials & secrets
.env
*.env
.env.*
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
secrets*
*.secret
*.token
*-token
*.key
*.pem
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.p12
*.pfx
*.gpg
# ...but DO ship the placeholder templates (no real values)
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Real Worker deploy config (the tracked wrangler.jsonc is a template)
wrangler.local.jsonc

# Internal records
admin/

# Names a live host. The units beside it ship, so they can be drift-checked.
multi/serve/SETUP.md

# Partner-specific commercial content. Tooling ships; personas written for one partner
# do not. Provision from a local copy via PERSONA_SOURCE.
agent/identity/IDEA_SCOUT.md

# Positioning about an upstream project we depend on, not documentation. Its durable
# technical claims are already in README.md and multi/README.md.
docs/multi-tenant-cross-agent-collaboration.md

# Retired experiments. broker/ publishes a deny-list where confine-member.sh uses an
# allowlist; hq/ drove state that has no provisioning path here, so no reader could run it.
deploy/broker/
deploy/hq/

# Operator-workstation tooling. Fleet operation ships (multi/serve/); tooling for one
# machine does not. The audience decides, not the content.
deploy/backup-laptop-agency.sh

# The same rule aimed at the deployment rather than the workstation: each of these needs the
# operator's own untracked env, their saved chat transcripts, or a live hostname before it
# means anything, so a reader of this repo can never run one. multi/verify/README.md said it
# of the first two already — they "prove nothing about the architecture that the suite above
# doesn't." Monitoring and maintenance, not evidence and not product.
multi/verify/test_instr_live.py
multi/verify/verify_live_isolation.py
deploy/repoint-hostname.sh

# Personas of agents that no longer run. These are data, not code, and provision-agent.sh
# revives one from a local copy via PERSONA_SOURCE — the same arrangement as IDEA_SCOUT
# above, so nothing is lost operationally. What a published inventory should describe is the
# fleet that IS, not the one that was. INTAKE is the clearest case: its experiment's tooling
# already left this repo, so the persona documented something a reader cannot find.
agent/identity/INTAKE.md
agent/identity/MULTIPLEX.md
agent/identity/OPS.md

# Unlanded: nothing on the client path calls it. Ship it when its caller ships.
multi/seam/handoff.py
multi/seam/test_handoff_2b.py

# Build / dependency / tool output
**/*.wasm
target/
node_modules/
.wrangler/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Named explicitly: pytest and ruff self-ignore via a .gitignore they write inside these,
# which is the tool's decision rather than a recorded one.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Logs & OS
*.log
.DS_Store
*.swp
